WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
Hank: Good morning, John.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.170
John: Good morning, Hank.

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:04.080
It's time for the Quadragocon.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.330
Hank: How are you liking your chances?

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.330
John: Uh, medium.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:15.719
I mean, if I were up against anyone but you,
I wouldn't like them at all.

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:21.250
[Hank laughs]

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:38.210
[Montage set to T-Shirt and Jeans by Hank
Green]

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:43.890
Hank: [laughs] Too scared.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:50.989
[Chariots of Fire theme plays]

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:56.290
Hank: I don't really know how croquet works.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.540
John: I think you just go through the wickets.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.579
OK, not bad.

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:02.670
Hank: [laughs] You missed, huh?

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:03.670
It's my turn now.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.670
No.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.670
No.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:06.670
John: No, no, no.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.670
Hank: My turn now.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:08.670
John: Hold on.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:09.670
Hank: You hit the ball and nothing happened.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.670
Oh, and you got both.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.840
John: That's what I wanted to do.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.760
Hank: You look like a dork.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.760
Oh, that's through.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.760
John: That's not through.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.010
Nope!

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.710
Hank: Oh!

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:23.409
John: No!

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:36.900
[Montage set to The Universe is Weird by Hank
Green]

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.350
Hank: Scott Westerfeld suggested a spitting
contest.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.560
I'm not going to spit, spit though, 'cause
it's gross.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.330
These have spittable things in them.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.830
Apple seeds.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.330
[Spitting noises]

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.009
Hank: Next round: typing quiz.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:53.009
Who types fastest?

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:54.330
John: I feel pretty confident.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.670
Hank: I also don't- do not feel good about
this round.

00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:59.690
[Typing noises]

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:04.979
John: I'm usually at over 100, but I've had
a few drinks.

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:06.160
Good luck to you, Hank.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.160
Hank: Okay.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.160
John: Alright, go.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.160
[Typing noises]

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.910
John: Three, two, one, I've got him right
at the end.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:11.910
He's 65!

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.319
Hank: Oh, oh, oh, oh God.

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:16.450
Hank from the future here.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.739
The first event in the Quadragocon, as we
said in John's video, was the Blue Steel competition,

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:24.770
and when we filmed this stuff, John's video
hadn't been uploaded yet, so we didn't know

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.220
who had won the Blue Steel competition.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.470
Well, it turns out, thank you all very much,
I did.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.840
I, by, like, a two-to-one margin, at least,
so I'm going to go ahead and give myself another

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.150
point, and we're going to play the last event
in the Quadragocon.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.470
John: Are you good at pool or bad?

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:37.470
Hank: I am not good.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.050
John: I'm also not good, so-

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.410
Hank: Okay, good, perfect.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:44.349
[Sound of hitting pool balls]

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:46.120
John: Oh, no!

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.300
Hank: Hurrr!

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.300
Uhhh!

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.300
Oh!

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.390
John: That's terrible news for me.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.360
Use this tiny little stick and I'm just going
to hit my balls as hard as I can.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.760
[Pool shots]

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.170
John: Woo!

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:59.810
Hank: Getting real close here at the end.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.940
John: This is basically all of Quadragocon
probably.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.459
Hank: Uhh!

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:05.459
Oooh!

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:07.489
John: Oh God.

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:09.010
Hank: Oh....

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.530
John: Heeeeeyyyyyaaaaah!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:14.319
Hank: How did that happen?

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:19.900
John: That's my whole strategy is to have
someone else screw up the 8 ball.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.909
Hank: I will say one thing for me that 8 ball
scratch rule, it's not a real rule, it's just

00:03:24.909 --> 00:03:27.030
a rule that we've always happened to play
by.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:31.950
If we're going with the actual official rules
the thing I did was not the end of the game.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.770
But as brothers we have always played that
if you scratch off the 8 ball you lose the

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.770
game.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.050
So anyway, that was Quadragocon 2015.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.640
I guess I don't mind tying with you John.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.780
I mean I do a little bit.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:44.260
It was really great to spend some time with
you and the family and to do some stuff together,

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.330
I miss you already, and I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:51.260
Because I wanted one a lot, for the next week
you can pre-order a Quadragocon 2015 shirt

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.989
and then never again so that's something that
you can do.

00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:56.350
John: Oh my God!

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.350
Hank: What!

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:58.350
What!

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.209
Uno points for style.

